course: dictionary
lesson: 14617
title: Popularly: common names and common beliefs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Popularly» is an adverb. It tells you how something is known, called or believed by most ordinary people. «The flower is popularly called the bluebell» means most people use the name bluebell for it, even if scientists use a longer name.
explain: The word has a second meaning, about voting. «The mayor was popularly elected» means the people chose her by voting.
explain: Be careful with «popularly believed». «It is popularly believed that bats are blind» sounds like a fact, but it only tells you that many people think it. Popularly does not make something true. Check the facts before you trust a common belief.
fact: Popularly means by most ordinary people, or in the way many people say it.
fact: «Popularly called» means the everyday name of something.
fact: «Popularly elected» means chosen by the votes of the people.
fact: «Sirius is popularly known as the Dog Star.» Most people use this nickname for it.
fact: «Popularly believed» can mean a common belief that is not always true.
exercise: «The tall tree is popularly called the oak.» What does popularly mean here? | In a secret way that only scientists know | *In the way most people name it | In the way the tree was painted | By one person in a single book
exercise: «The council was popularly elected by the voters.» How were the councillors chosen? | *By votes from the people | By drawing names from a hat | By the head teacher | By the king alone
exercise: Sam says, «It is popularly believed that goldfish have a three-second memory.» What should Sam remember? | It is a fact that every scientist has proved | *Many people believe it, but it may not be true | Popularly means it is a secret | Popularly means it is always true
test: Which sentence uses popularly to mean chosen by votes? | The bus popularly stopped at the gate | He popularly sang in the shower | *The mayor was popularly elected by the town | The cat popularly slept on the mat
test: «Sirius is popularly known as the Dog Star.» What does this tell you? | It is the name used in a maths test | It means Sirius is a real dog | *It is the name most people use for it | It is a secret name only astronomers know
exam: Which word means "in the way most people say it"? | quietly | *popularly | barely | exactly
